    "quote": "Boilerplate removal is the step that strips a page's repeated surroundings (navigation, footers, ads, consent notices, related-article panels) and keeps the main content. Every method does this by guessing, so every method has failure modes. Below: what gets removed, how the main approaches decide, what they wrongly discard, and how to test one before it feeds a RAG or LLM pipeline.",
